    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0195" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg79"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11/538.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the
                            Acting Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: You may be interested to
                    know that the contemplated action of the American Government in returning to
                    China the unused portion of the indemnity payments for the maintenance of the
                    student movement between China and the United States has called forth
                    expressions of gratitude from all quarters in Peking. I need hardly assure you
                    that China will never forget this generous act of the American Government. The
                    provisions thus made for the support of the Chinese students in this country are
                    amply sufficient for the next two years.</p>
                <p>With assurance [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kai Fu Shah</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
